  "source_and_output_review": [
    {
      "rule": "Private diagnostic retention remains durable after projection finishes or latest-run changes; deletion requires an expired owned run and a durable result, and cannot erase result or public history.",
      "files": [
        "lib/run.mjs",
        "lib/execution.mjs",
        "lib/tick.mjs",
        "lib/run_log.mjs",
        "test/execution-backends.test.mjs",
        "docs/execution.md"
      ],
      "boundaries_checked": [
        "prepareStart persists completed private runs before successor pointer replacement; the shared execution caller still invokes it before paid intent or allowance accounting.",
        "The existing version 1 queue retains drained and empty private runs and backlog runs that finish projection, rotating one old run alongside the current run.",
        "Drained cursors skip diagnostic file reads and journal writes. Bounded page, record and buffer limits remain unchanged; unrelated progress and GitHub review still advance.",
        "Read-only current/status/tail/history calls do not ingest raw diagnostics, mutate the queue or perform expiry cleanup.",
        "Expiry removes only provider.log and sensitive-redactions.json once result.json exists. A delayed result preserves both files and queue eligibility even after expiry.",
        "A deletion failure leaves its durable queue item for coordinator retry. Partial cleanup and already missing files remain safe through force removal of files, without recursive deletion.",
        "Missing or truncated diagnostics and missing redaction metadata emit stable gaps and retain any remaining private file for cleanup. Missing metadata uses the owned job start for its 24-hour expiry and cannot authorize raw projection.",
        "Results, session, recorded job exit, public log bytes, replay IDs and latest-run remain intact across cleanup and restart.",
        "Invalid cursors, unsupported queue versions and queue write failures still prevent a new paid intent without changing ownership or allowance.",
        "The compatible version 1 queue does not rediscover directories an older package already omitted; documented explicit maintenance checks expiry and cached results and removes only the two private files.",
        "No transport availability, model/provider defaults, credentials, paid-call scope, execution permissions or human merge boundary changed."
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "drained and empty local runs remain queued for private retention cleanup across successors and restart",
        "private local cleanup retries removal failures without dropping its durable queue entry",
        "completed local output survives a successor, restart and cursor replay with exact paginated history",
        "large queued local output uses bounded round-robin pages while unrelated jobs and review advance",
        "queued local output has explicit stable gaps for expiry, missing diagnostics and missing redaction metadata",
        "incompatible local projection state prevents paid intent and preserves ownership and allowance",
        "oversized local records discard every suffix across queued restart, replay and legacy cursors with bounded reads"
      ]
    }
  ],
